MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Different Shades Of Blue feels like a natural next listen because I want more of the blues guitar that drew me to Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "Ride Out, Life Journey and Duets feel relevant because their roots-oriented or soulful character connects with what interested me in Memphis."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Cheek to Cheek offers vocal jazz standards, which do not satisfy my current desire for blues guitar and roots rock.",
    "A Christopher Cross Christmas misses my current listening purpose because I am not seeking seasonal music, while Pet Sounds emphasizes orchestrated pop rather than the blues sound I want today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad interest in established artists as enough, even when their musical styles lead to very different listening experiences.",
    "Familiar classic albums seem to receive more emphasis than my interest in finding another release to explore; Led Zeppelin IV appeals to me, but it is not my choice today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels matters especially today: I am looking for expressive blues guitar, not just music from familiar artists.",
    "I rarely make several selections in one visit. Reflective songwriting, melodic rock and soulful performances can all interest me without competing with my first choice of a blues album today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in roots, soul and classic rock, but only partly capture my current preference for discovering a blues-guitar release."
}
